# Introduction

Books group related material into ordered chapters. The methods we use are
introduced in the next part, and @fig-structure sketches how the parts follow
one another.

![How this book's chapters build on one another.](structure.svg){#fig-structure}

## Background

Some background, with a little inline math $e^{i\pi}+1=0$ to check rendering. The
identity behind it is worth naming, because @eq-euler is referred to again in the
next part:

$$ e^{i\theta} = \cos\theta + i\sin\theta $$ {#eq-euler}
